{
  "_field_reference": "Airside Machine AI competitor roster (data/competitors.json). Loaded by engine/ai.py on startup. Underscore keys are documentation only — the engine ignores them.\n\nFILE-LEVEL\n  competitors          Array of airline definitions (required).\n\nIDENTITY (required on each entry)\n  competitor_id        Unique key, format AI_<TOKEN> (e.g. AI_TITAN). Never change after a save has seeded this airline.\n  name                 Display name shown in UI/news.\n  callsign             Exactly 3 letters (e.g. TTN). Used on the flight board.\n  home_hub_iata        Hub airport IATA code. Must exist in data/airports.csv unless hub_airport is provided.\n\nSTARTING TREASURY & FLEET (only applied when the airline is first inserted into a save)\n  cash                 Starting cash in USD. Typical ranges: budget 15–40M, major 50–150M, mega ~600M. Existing saves keep live cash — edits here do not reset it.\n  fleet_size           Number of aircraft tails created in ai_fleet at seed time. Typical 5–45; megas up to ~120.\n\nSTRATEGY & PERSONALITY (refreshed from JSON on every startup for existing airlines)\n  strategy             Route logic template. One of:\n                         HUBSPOKE — hub-and-spoke pairs from home_hub_iata (default).\n                         BUDGET — short/medium cartesian network, capped ~1500 nm.\n                         PREMIUM — long-haul between large airports (score ≥ 600k).\n                         POINTTOPOINT — non-hub pairs within hub radius.\n  aggressiveness       0.7–2.0. Scales gate/slot auction bid sizes. ≥1.5 treated as aggressive growth style fallback.\n  risk_tolerance       0.3–0.85. Higher opens riskier routes (lowers score threshold). Budget carriers usually 0.75–0.85.\n  expansion_rate       1–12. Base cap on new routes opened per full evaluation week (stance adds +0–2). Megas often 12.\n  reputation           ~50–92. Drives brand_power at seed/refresh (higher = stronger demand capture).\n\nWEEKLY BUDGETS\n  weekly_route_budget  USD spent per week opening routes (acquisition + setup). Typical 300k–2.5M.\n  weekly_slot_budget   USD spent per week on runway slot auctions. Typical 100k–1.5M.\n  bid_probability      0.0–1.0. Chance the AI bids on a gate/slot auction each week. Aggressive 0.7–0.95.\n\nFLEET CAP\n  max_fleet_size       Hard upper bound on total tails (fleet growth stops here). Typical 14–24; megas up to 120.\n\nSTARTER NETWORK (only applied when the airline has zero routes in the save)\n  starter_spokes       Array of 4–8 destination IATA codes the airline would realistically fly from the hub. Include international spokes (LHR, NRT) for intercontinental carriers.\n  starter_count        How many spokes to seed from the list. Clamped 3–6 (default 3).\n  starter_frequency    Weekly frequency on each starter route. 1–7 (typical 2–3; megas 5).\n\nINTERNATIONAL EXPANSION (optional)\n  international        true — enables intercontinental candidate search (default radius 5600 nm), biases pool toward gated trophy airports, seeds ~55% narrow / 45% wide fleet mix, and bonuses long-haul scoring. Use for US/Asia/Europe megacarriers.\n  international_radius_nm  Optional override when international is true. Default 5600. PREMIUM without this flag still gets 4200 nm.\n  hub_radius_nm        Optional per-airline override for candidate search radius (nm). Rare; overrides financial_constants ai_hub_radius_nm (default 2500).\n\nGROWTH (object — optional; defaults derived from strategy/aggressiveness)\n  growth.style         aggressive | measured | selective. Affects deepen rate, exit grace, and stance expansion bonus (+2 vs +1 routes in GROW stance).\n  growth.deepen_per_eval   1–8. How many profitable existing routes get +1 frequency per evaluation. Aggressive 2–8.\n  growth.extra_exit_grace_weeks  0–6. Extra loss weeks before a route is closed. Selective 4–6; aggressive 2–3.\n  growth.require_flown_pnl_to_exit  true/false. If true, route must have flown P&L before exit rules apply (default true).\n  growth.fleet_growth_per_eval  1–4. Max new tails leased per evaluation when cash/backlog allows. Megas 4.\n\nHUB AIRPORT (optional — only if home_hub_iata is missing from airports.csv)\n  hub_airport          Object with: icao, name, city, country, lat, lon, runway_length_ft, gate_count, timezone, score, category (large_airport | medium_airport).\n\nLIVE SAVE FIELDS (in SQLite competitors table — do NOT put in JSON)\n  stance, stance_since_week, consecutive_loss_weeks, last_evaluation_week, brand_power (derived), actual routes in competitor_routes, live cash after week 1.\n\nREFRESH BEHAVIOUR\n  New competitor_id → inserted with cash, fleet, starter routes, and hub gates on next --ui start.\n  Existing competitor_id → only personality/budget knobs refresh; cash, fleet count, and network are untouched.",
